- **CLI Commands**: Enhance `list-tasks` with flags: `--status <pending|completed>`, `--priority <low|medium|high>`, `--tag <tag>`, `--search <text>`. Add `view-task <id>` for detailed single-task output. Use minimist or Bun-native parsing for flag handling in the dispatcher.
- **Filtering Logic**: In handlers, load tasks via `loadTasks()`, then apply chainable filters (e.g., `tasks.filter(t => !status || t.status === status)` for each criterion). For free-text search, check if description includes the search string (case-insensitive). Output filtered tasks as JSON array to console.
- **Viewing**: For `view-task`, load tasks, find by ID, and output as JSON object or throw error if not found.
- **Code Structure**:
  ```typescript
  // src/models/task.ts (updated)
  export interface Task {
    id: string;
    description: string;
    status: 'pending' | 'completed';
    priority?: 'low' | 'medium' | 'high';
    tags: string[];
    createdAt: string;
  }

  // src/index.ts (example handler)
  import minimist from 'minimist'; // Lightweight for flag parsing

  commands['list-tasks'] = async (args) => {
    const opts = minimist(args);
    const tasks = await loadTasks('tasks.json');
    let filtered = tasks;
    if (opts.status) filtered = filtered.filter(t => t.status === opts.status);
    if (opts.priority) filtered = filtered.filter(t => t.priority === opts.priority);
    if (opts.tag) filtered = filtered.filter(t => t.tags.includes(opts.tag));
    if (opts.search) filtered = filtered.filter(t => t.description.toLowerCase().includes(opts.search.toLowerCase()));
    console.log(JSON.stringify(filtered, null, 2));
  };

  commands['view-task'] = async (args) => {
    const id = args[0];
    const tasks = await loadTasks('tasks.json');
    const task = tasks.find(t => t.id === id);
    if (task) console.log(JSON.stringify(task, null, 2));
    else console.error('Task not found');
